{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426932-token-cost-and-refinement-help","id":426932,"title":"Token cost and refinement help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-03T13:38:47-08:00","id":426932,"title":"Token cost and refinement help","content":"The concept is simple: an old-fashioned church key (warded lock key, properly) which can be inserted into any mechanical lock, which will allow the door to open into a single, specific Hollow. Dark, glossy metal mien, dull, rough mask. Not sure what the drawback and catch should be. Maybe the door in question continues to lead to the Hollow for a certain period? Though I have no idea at all of what might make a suitable catch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 03-03-2015, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T22:54:20-08:00","id":427470,"title":"","content":"That sounds allot like Ritual Doorway (RoS, pg 95) which allows you to have a short ritual &quot;key&quot; that will open any door into your hollow. Do you see this key opening to the same hollow every time or does the user specify where they want to go? If it's the former I'd lean towards the Ritual Doorway solution where the key is not magical at all but is simply a tool used in the ritual for that hollow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T06:46:54-08:00","id":427665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>helel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426932-token-cost-and-refinement-help?p=427470#post427470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds allot like Ritual Doorway (RoS, pg 95) which allows you to have a short ritual &amp;quot;key&amp;quot; that will open any door into your hollow. Do you see this key opening to the same hollow every time or does the user specify where they want to go? If it's the former I'd lean towards the Ritual Doorway solution where the key is not magical at all but is simply a tool used in the ritual for that hollow.</div> </div> </div> </div>The key would only lead to one Hollow. I'd forgotten about Ritual Doorway; that does sound like a better approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T22:40:56-08:00","id":431072,"title":"","content":"Upon rereading the merit in question, I decided a Token is indeed the way to go. Here's what I have:<br /> <br /> Lockless Key (\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> This heavy black church key can be inserted into any mechanical lock and turned. If the lock is in a door, that door becomes a hedge gate that leads to a Hollow chosen at the time of the key's creation. The key's user can then step through the door as normal for a Hollow door. This connection is temporary, not a permanent increase in the Hollow's Doors rating. Note that the if the key is used on a locked door, the door remains locked.<br /> <br /> Action: Standard<br /> Mien: The Lockless Key looks new rather than old and worn. But it's still a heavy black key.<br /> Drawback: The gate created, though temporary, persists much longer than normal: One minute per point of the user's Wyrd after use ceases rather than one turn per point.<br /> Catch: The key is inserted in a locked lock, which the changeling forces open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T16:20:57-08:00","id":431964,"title":"","content":"That certainly works. I like the catch especially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T05:19:07-07:00","id":432526,"title":"","content":"The Catch for a Token is generally an extra bit of harm or drawback that the character must endure in order to use the Token for free. Something like &quot;The character unavoidably cuts her hand open while using the token, taking a point of Lethal damage that can't be reduced by any means&quot; or &quot;The character develops an obsession with the key, developing the Fixation derangement for the next 24 hours.&quot; <br /> <br /> In addition, I'd make the Drawback a bit more stringent. Not only does the gate last longer, but it throws up a beacon to anything that can see through the Mask (or alternately, subconsciously calls to mortals in a certain range). Leads to more Plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T07:35:44-07:00","id":432613,"title":"","content":"It is true that the catches in the book are mostly &quot;take a Lethal&quot; but that is boring. IMO catches that require specific action or conditions, that is to say catches that work like contract catches, are much more interesting.<br /> <br /> As for the drawback, that is already pretty severe. It lasts plenty long enough for somebody to stumble upon it. If the key was stronger and could be used to access any hollow the user choses then it might need more but this is a very specialized token. Heck, for everyone save the rightful owner it effectively has the drawback &quot;you're walking into an unknown hollow with unknown wards. Good luck.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T16:43:14-07:00","id":433271,"title":"","content":"I agree. A token's catch should relate in some way to its function and the creator's nature. The key's creator is an ogre, hence the brute force catch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}